  intro:
    "A graph is an equation you can see. On 4MA1 Higher papers you will be asked to complete a table and plot a quadratic or cubic, recognise curves from their shape, use a graph to solve an equation that has no neat answer, read speeds and distances off real-life graphs, and describe how a curve moves when its equation changes. These questions are often worth 4–6 marks each, and almost all of the marks are for careful, systematic work rather than clever tricks. Master the methods here and the whole Algebra strand becomes more visual — and much easier to check.",
